  "body": "Maintainer request from #1452 (\"We should be able to load DXF file to do profile cuts on.\").\n\nDepends on #1860.\n\n## Goal\nExtend the `crates/geometry/src/dxf/` reader from #1860 to parse `SPLINE`, `ELLIPSE`, and bounded `BLOCK`/`INSERT` entities cleanly.\n\n## Scope\n- Parse `ELLIPSE` (center, major endpoint, axis ratio, start/end parameters, extrusion vector check) from Autodesk's published DXF Reference. Return exact `Circle`/`Arc` primitives when the axis ratio equals `1.0` within tolerance, and flatten non-circular ellipses adaptively within a caller chord tolerance in millimeters.\n- Parse `SPLINE` (degree, flags, knot vector, control points, fit points, rational weights). Evaluate rational and non-rational B-splines via de Boor's algorithm and subdivide adaptively so chord deviation stays within the caller tolerance. Recover circular arcs when the spline matches a circle within tolerance. Reject malformed knot counts, negative weights, or non-finite control points by name.\n- Pass the flattening chord tolerance through `ImportDxf` (#1862) and record it on import metadata.\n- Parse `BLOCKS` definitions and expand `INSERT` references (translation, rotation, uniform X/Y scale, row/column array grids, and `0`-layer inheritance per DXF rules).\n- Enforce strict recursion depth, total expanded entity count, and cycle detection caps against block bombs. Refuse cyclic references, external references (`XREF`), non-uniform X/Y shear scaling, or tilted OCS extrusions by block/entity name.\n\n## Done means\nDense point sampling proves flattened `SPLINE` and `ELLIPSE` polylines stay within the stated tolerance in millimeters; circular splines and ellipses keep exact `Arc`/`Circle` segments; `INSERT` expands uniform blocks (and nested blocks within limits) accurately; cyclic blocks, sheared inserts, xrefs, and malformed splines return named errors with passing fuzz tests.\n\nPart of #1452\n",
